1
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:43,959
Morning...

2
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:46,209
Huh? Leaving so early?

3
00:00:46,210 --> 00:00:48,880
Just remembered some work stuff.

4
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:52,700
And here I was gonna make breakfast today.

5
00:00:53,260 --> 00:00:54,760
Remember to lock the door.

6
00:00:55,630 --> 00:00:56,970
Got it.

7
00:00:58,980 --> 00:01:00,080
Oh, right, tomorrow...

8
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:06,320
I have a business trip.

9
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:11,270
What happened that day three years ago...

10
00:01:12,840 --> 00:01:14,560
He's probably forgotten all about it.

11
00:01:15,900 --> 00:01:18,379
It's fine, don't worry about it.

12
00:01:18,380 --> 00:01:21,370
Kawakita-san from
General Affairs is really great.

13
00:01:22,370 --> 00:01:24,120
Mizoguchi, set up a mixer for us!

14
00:01:24,910 --> 00:01:27,019
No way, ask her out yourself.

15
00:01:27,020 --> 00:01:29,180
Come on, I'll invite your crush too.

16
00:01:34,080 --> 00:01:36,790
With a reaction like that,
there really is someone!

17
00:01:37,980 --> 00:01:39,080
Who is it?

18
00:01:41,480 --> 00:01:43,880
From Sales... Kobayashi.

19
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:45,899
Seriously?

20
00:01:45,900 --> 00:01:48,289
Kobayashi, huh?

21
00:01:48,290 --> 00:01:50,369
Kobayashi...

22
00:01:50,370 --> 00:01:51,719
Huh?

23
00:01:51,720 --> 00:01:52,899
Does he have a girlfriend?

24
00:01:52,900 --> 00:01:55,420
No, he has a boyfriend.

25
00:01:56,280 --> 00:01:57,949
I'm only saying this
because he's open about it.

26
00:01:57,950 --> 00:01:59,210
He's gay.

27
00:02:00,980 --> 00:02:02,080
Oh, I see...

28
00:02:02,960 --> 00:02:05,370
Either way, he seems super popular.

29
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:08,620
Right...

30
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,349
What about you, Kanda?
Who would you ask out?

31
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:16,299
Huh? Me?

32
00:02:16,300 --> 00:02:18,040
Well, I...

33
00:02:19,020 --> 00:02:20,470
I'm gonna hit the restroom.

34
00:02:22,980 --> 00:02:25,020
I wonder what Kanda's deal is.

35
00:02:29,480 --> 00:02:30,480
Makes you curious.

36
00:02:31,440 --> 00:02:33,330
Hey, are you okay?

37
00:02:37,070 --> 00:02:38,280
Are you drunk?

38
00:02:46,330 --> 00:02:47,280
Listen...

39
00:02:47,281 --> 00:02:48,420
Yeah?

40
00:02:50,920 --> 00:02:53,350
I'm actually gay.

41
00:02:57,320 --> 00:03:00,690
So sometimes I can't just
play along with everyone.

42
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:05,950
Sorry for keeping it from you.

43
00:03:09,900 --> 00:03:10,900
Oh, really?

44
00:03:14,220 --> 00:03:16,020
Why are you apologizing, though?

45
00:03:16,980 --> 00:03:18,630
There's nothing to be sorry about.

46
00:03:23,380 --> 00:03:24,380
Thanks.

47
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:26,080
Yeah.

48
00:03:29,960 --> 00:03:31,560
Don't worry, though.

49
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:35,289
You're not my type.

50
00:03:35,290 --> 00:03:38,210
Nothing's ever gonna happen between us.

51
00:03:40,420 --> 00:03:41,690
Well...

52
00:03:43,320 --> 00:03:45,319
He was just trying to make
me feel comfortable, right?

53
00:03:45,320 --> 00:03:46,850
With what he just said.

54
00:03:47,840 --> 00:03:48,840
But even so...

55
00:03:53,620 --> 00:03:56,870
Did he have to shut it down that hard?

56
00:04:56,880 --> 00:04:59,340
"You Should Be The One To Come Kiss Me"

57
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:04,360
(Episode 3) True to his word,
three years have passed since then.

58
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,260
And between Ueno and me...

59
00:05:07,460 --> 00:05:08,840
nothing ever happened.

60
00:05:12,380 --> 00:05:15,440
Nothing happening at all
is only natural, right?

61
00:05:17,080 --> 00:05:18,080
Oh.

62
00:05:20,433 --> 00:05:22,513
[Generic ad copy]

63
00:05:33,520 --> 00:05:34,520
Hey.

64
00:05:35,800 --> 00:05:37,000
Ueno, do you...

65
00:05:38,240 --> 00:05:41,310
like this TAKUMI guy from F:IVE?

66
00:05:45,550 --> 00:05:46,580
Why do you ask?

67
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:51,510
Because your watch history
is nothing but his videos.

68
00:05:55,540 --> 00:05:56,540
Not really.

69
00:06:00,190 --> 00:06:01,190
Just...

70
00:06:02,180 --> 00:06:04,000
I don't dislike him.

71
00:06:08,780 --> 00:06:12,149
Besides, the only reason
Ueno is friends with me

72
00:06:12,150 --> 00:06:14,320
is because I'm not his type.

73
00:06:19,880 --> 00:06:23,320
(I'm TAKUMI from the vocal group F:IVE.
Sharing lots of solo stuff and music content!)

74
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:30,010
He liked so many of his posts.

75
00:06:31,020 --> 00:06:33,380
He's clearly super into him.

76
00:06:38,840 --> 00:06:40,040
Soft and cute.

77
00:06:41,020 --> 00:06:42,220
Puppy-dog type.

78
00:06:43,150 --> 00:06:44,900
Artistic vibe...

79
00:06:56,540 --> 00:06:58,320
Not like me at all.

80
00:07:00,080 --> 00:07:01,770
Not that I care, though.

81
00:07:12,400 --> 00:07:13,930
Wait, Kanda-san.

82
00:07:14,800 --> 00:07:16,329
Did you get a perm?

83
00:07:16,330 --> 00:07:17,549
Yeah.

84
00:07:17,550 --> 00:07:19,739
- It looks great on you.
- Thanks.

85
00:07:19,740 --> 00:07:23,480
By the way, I heard Ueno-san
is getting transferred.

86
00:07:34,740 --> 00:07:35,840
Thanks.

87
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:42,850
How come I didn't hear about your transfer?

88
00:07:43,630 --> 00:07:44,790
Oh.

89
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:46,549
Guess I didn't tell you.

90
00:07:46,550 --> 00:07:48,090
Man...

91
00:07:49,180 --> 00:07:51,020
That's cold, man.

92
00:07:53,140 --> 00:07:54,780
Why make a big deal out of it?

93
00:07:55,480 --> 00:07:56,930
It's not like I'm quitting.

94
00:07:58,580 --> 00:08:00,120
Why now, though?

95
00:08:02,340 --> 00:08:04,860
Heard someone's leaving due to illness.

96
00:08:05,540 --> 00:08:07,250
They've been looking for a replacement.

97
00:08:08,690 --> 00:08:10,750
Figured it'd suit me better than sales.

98
00:08:11,420 --> 00:08:12,420
I see.

99
00:08:19,440 --> 00:08:21,740
You're a natural at sales. Keep it up.

100
00:08:29,240 --> 00:08:30,240
Oh.

101
00:08:30,241 --> 00:08:31,420
By the way...

102
00:08:32,200 --> 00:08:33,590
Did you get a perm?

103
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:36,720
Oh, yeah.

104
00:08:37,940 --> 00:08:38,940
I did.

105
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:42,600
Looks good.

106
00:09:29,060 --> 00:09:30,060
Huh?

107
00:09:30,820 --> 00:09:32,030
Hair wax...

108
00:09:39,360 --> 00:09:40,360
Ah.

109
00:09:40,950 --> 00:09:42,090
It's at Ueno's place.

110
00:09:50,210 --> 00:09:54,480
If we're just friends, there's no
need to style myself to his taste.

111
00:09:56,400 --> 00:10:00,950
Getting a perm and styling it
every morning is such a hassle.

112
00:10:04,140 --> 00:10:05,140
Even so...

113
00:10:05,880 --> 00:10:07,700
Couldn't he at least notice me a little?

114
00:10:08,600 --> 00:10:09,770
Just me, as a person.

115
00:10:13,060 --> 00:10:14,400
Even if someone isn't your type,

116
00:10:15,180 --> 00:10:17,530
you can still fall for the
person sitting next to you.

117
00:10:19,860 --> 00:10:21,659
Couldn't he...

118
00:10:21,660 --> 00:10:24,970
fall for me like that, too?

119
00:10:49,960 --> 00:10:50,960
I feel like...

120
00:10:52,060 --> 00:10:54,020
I just dreamed about Ueno.

121
00:11:04,440 --> 00:11:07,119
Welcome back. You look sleepy.

122
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,380
I'm back.

123
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:10,040
And good morning.

124
00:11:11,120 --> 00:11:13,060
How was the business trip to Sendai?

125
00:11:13,820 --> 00:11:16,379
I brought back zunda mochi as a souvenir.

126
00:11:16,380 --> 00:11:17,760
Thanks.

127
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:19,859
Should I put it in the
break room for everyone?

128
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,130
Yeah, thanks.

129
00:11:25,010 --> 00:11:25,680
Not this bag, though.

130
00:11:25,681 --> 00:11:26,760
This is a personal gift.

131
00:11:27,660 --> 00:11:28,660
Gotcha.

132
00:11:49,120 --> 00:11:51,120
Can I come over tonight?

133
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:58,550
Sorry.

134
00:11:58,551 --> 00:12:01,020
Don't come over until the end of the month.

135
00:12:04,090 --> 00:12:05,030
Huh?

136
00:12:05,031 --> 00:12:07,860
I have a friend staying over.

137
00:12:16,320 --> 00:12:17,650
A friend...

138
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:29,079
Regarding supply volume, we'd
like to maintain the status quo

139
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:31,750
as we move forward with this project.

140
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:34,670
Ethan, what do you think?

141
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:36,420
Yeah that works.

142
00:12:36,854 --> 00:12:37,466
OK.

143
00:12:38,920 --> 00:12:40,499
Alright, please proceed with this plan.

144
00:12:40,500 --> 00:12:41,719
Yes, understood.

145
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:43,130
Thank you very much.

146
00:12:46,090 --> 00:12:47,260
A friend...

147
00:12:48,460 --> 00:12:49,809
When you eat a chocolate cornet,

148
00:12:49,810 --> 00:12:52,329
you definitely have to start from the head.

149
00:12:52,330 --> 00:12:54,910
It's the golden ratio
of bread and chocolate!

150
00:12:55,560 --> 00:12:57,520
Taking a big bite right here...

151
00:13:02,160 --> 00:13:03,400
A friend...

152
00:13:04,860 --> 00:13:05,860
is it?

153
00:13:14,600 --> 00:13:16,240
It happens from time to time.

154
00:13:17,080 --> 00:13:18,640
Periods when he won't let me come over.

155
00:13:19,980 --> 00:13:20,980
And yet...

156
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:25,920
Whenever I go back later, I
always pick up on little clues.

157
00:13:33,640 --> 00:13:36,650
Spotless floors.

158
00:13:37,560 --> 00:13:38,980
Freshly washed sheets.

159
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:42,630
And incense burning, as if to
cover up a trace of someone.

160
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:52,120
Probably a friend with benefits.

161
00:13:57,040 --> 00:13:59,220
Kanda-san looks so deep in thought.

162
00:14:00,920 --> 00:14:02,020
He's so hot.

163
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:06,090
The Lanau project seems really tough.

164
00:14:06,620 --> 00:14:08,190
He must be figuring out his next move.

165
00:14:10,430 --> 00:14:13,520
If he got a boyfriend, he'd
take back my spare key.

166
00:14:19,360 --> 00:14:21,420
Might as well just give
this to him at the office.

167
00:14:29,080 --> 00:14:31,030
Just got back from my Sendai trip.

168
00:14:38,330 --> 00:14:39,379
(Souvenir)

169
00:14:39,380 --> 00:14:40,460
Kanda-san.

170
00:14:41,260 --> 00:14:42,460
Do you have a minute?

171
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,759
I'd love your advice on the
internal pitch competition.

172
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,220
Oh, sure.

173
00:14:47,760 --> 00:14:49,570
Let's see...

174
00:14:54,640 --> 00:14:55,850
Kobayashi.

175
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:57,800
Yes?

176
00:15:00,100 --> 00:15:01,540
If you're free, how about tonight?

177
00:15:04,260 --> 00:15:05,260
Huh?

178
00:15:05,840 --> 00:15:06,840
Oh.

179
00:15:06,841 --> 00:15:08,761
Just the two of us might
come off as harassment.

180
00:15:11,300 --> 00:15:12,300
What?

181
00:15:16,960 --> 00:15:18,869
You caught me off guard for a second there.

182
00:15:18,870 --> 00:15:21,210
Next time, just ask me out normally.

183
00:15:22,260 --> 00:15:23,459
How on earth did you ask him?

184
00:15:23,460 --> 00:15:26,049
Huh? Was it weird?

185
00:15:26,050 --> 00:15:28,920
Phrasing it like that is bad for my heart.

186
00:15:30,130 --> 00:15:32,850
- Excuse me, another draft beer.
- Coming right up.

187
00:15:34,140 --> 00:15:35,110
Drinking fast tonight.

188
00:15:35,111 --> 00:15:36,560
In the mood to drink?

189
00:15:38,960 --> 00:15:39,960
Not really...

190
00:15:41,100 --> 00:15:43,560
I asked Kanda-san for some
tips on the internal competition.

191
00:15:44,220 --> 00:15:45,359
It's that time of year already, huh?

192
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:48,089
Lucky for me, we have a
former champion right here.

193
00:15:48,090 --> 00:15:50,489
- True.
- Excuse me, here's your draft beer.

194
00:15:50,490 --> 00:15:51,739
Thanks.

195
00:15:51,740 --> 00:15:52,740
Sorry, actually...

196
00:15:56,080 --> 00:15:57,080
There's something I...

197
00:15:57,700 --> 00:15:59,140
wanted to ask you, too, Kobayashi.

198
00:16:00,180 --> 00:16:01,180
What's up?

199
00:16:06,920 --> 00:16:10,650
Is it possible to see a straight
friend as a romantic interest?

200
00:16:14,380 --> 00:16:15,380
Oh.

201
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:17,890
It's not impossible.

202
00:16:18,850 --> 00:16:19,949
I've dated a straight guy before.

203
00:16:19,950 --> 00:16:20,930
Wait, seriously?

204
00:16:20,931 --> 00:16:23,050
How did that even happen?

205
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Well...

206
00:16:26,001 --> 00:16:27,319
Way too close!

207
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,580
Back up a little.

208
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:32,280
- Oh...
- My bad...

209
00:16:35,620 --> 00:16:36,819
Back when I was a student...

210
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:41,310
It started out as a joke, but then he
suddenly said he wanted to try it with a guy.

211
00:16:42,500 --> 00:16:43,660
And one thing led to another.

212
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,710
Led to what?

213
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,690
You know...

214
00:16:52,120 --> 00:16:54,420
Oh, don't mind me. Go right ahead.

215
00:16:57,346 --> 00:16:58,715
After we slept together,

216
00:16:58,930 --> 00:17:00,730
it just naturally turned
into a relationship.

217
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:08,500
So you're saying...

218
00:17:09,360 --> 00:17:12,540
he developed feelings for
you after sleeping together?

219
00:17:14,100 --> 00:17:15,100
I mean,

220
00:17:15,720 --> 00:17:20,090
if you're gonna date a straight guy, isn't
sleeping together the first real hurdle?

221
00:17:25,420 --> 00:17:29,479
He didn't think he could do
it, but it turned out he could.

222
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:33,230
So we figured we'd give dating a shot.

223
00:17:38,560 --> 00:17:39,860
Sleeping together, huh...

224
00:17:40,940 --> 00:17:41,940
Wait, what?

225
00:17:42,900 --> 00:17:44,950
So that really is what
it all comes down to...

226
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,740
What on earth is he talking about?

227
00:17:54,700 --> 00:17:55,820
What's up with Kanda?

228
00:18:00,040 --> 00:18:01,580
Just leave him be.

229
00:18:05,460 --> 00:18:07,539
- Excuse me!
- Yes, coming right up!

230
00:18:07,540 --> 00:18:09,420
- I'll take another one.
- Sure thing.

231
00:18:16,080 --> 00:18:17,280
Morning.

232
00:18:18,320 --> 00:18:19,320
Good morning.

233
00:18:19,480 --> 00:18:20,480
Morning.

234
00:18:22,220 --> 00:18:24,060
Oh, morning.

235
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:27,780
I'm here for the edamame mochi.

236
00:18:32,110 --> 00:18:33,679
Again?

237
00:18:33,680 --> 00:18:36,070
(Advance Expense Settlement
Form - Entertainment Expenses.)

238
00:18:37,990 --> 00:18:40,450
(Advance Expense Summary
Sheet - Settled by: Kanda Eito.)

239
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,360
Oh, there's only one left.

240
00:18:47,060 --> 00:18:48,060
Lucky you.

241
00:18:49,660 --> 00:18:51,320
I'll take this as your apology.

242
00:18:52,220 --> 00:18:53,220
Apology for what?

243
00:18:55,420 --> 00:18:57,070
Don't talk to Kobayashi about romance

244
00:18:58,300 --> 00:19:01,520
right in front of me.

245
00:19:06,850 --> 00:19:08,299
Wait, you still have feelings for him?

246
00:19:08,300 --> 00:19:10,440
Hold on, but Kobayashi is...

247
00:19:10,980 --> 00:19:11,980
I know.

248
00:19:12,700 --> 00:19:13,700
I've already given up.

249
00:19:14,540 --> 00:19:16,499
But human feelings don't work like that.

250
00:19:16,500 --> 00:19:19,569
You can't just go, "Oh, I see,
guess I'll stop liking him then,"

251
00:19:19,570 --> 00:19:22,410
and magically move on.

252
00:19:23,950 --> 00:19:24,950
Fair point...

253
00:19:26,300 --> 00:19:28,679
Wait, wasn't that three years ago, though?

254
00:19:28,680 --> 00:19:30,080
Yeah.

255
00:19:33,420 --> 00:19:34,420
Seriously...

256
00:19:34,960 --> 00:19:37,340
Even I think I'm pathetic.

257
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Jeez.

258
00:19:39,560 --> 00:19:40,680
I'm really sorry about that.

259
00:19:41,920 --> 00:19:43,520
Why don't you just confess to him, then?

260
00:19:44,010 --> 00:19:45,969
Just walk right into a rejection?

261
00:19:45,970 --> 00:19:47,949
At least it'd give you some closure.

262
00:19:47,950 --> 00:19:49,960
Maybe it would for me,

263
00:19:51,060 --> 00:19:52,839
but that'd just put
Kobayashi in an awkward spot.

264
00:19:52,840 --> 00:19:55,670
Getting confessed to by
someone who knows he's gay.

265
00:19:58,900 --> 00:19:59,900
Yeah, I guess.

266
00:20:04,160 --> 00:20:05,700
That sounds rough.

267
00:20:07,040 --> 00:20:08,549
It is rough!

268
00:20:08,550 --> 00:20:09,779
Yeah.

269
00:20:09,780 --> 00:20:11,920
- What am I supposed to do?!
- Ow!

270
00:20:12,460 --> 00:20:13,699
How should I know?

271
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,039
Stop hitting me, that hurts!

272
00:20:15,040 --> 00:20:19,169
- Do you get it now? It's complicated!
- I'm really sorry, I apologize!

273
00:20:19,170 --> 00:20:21,439
So just hear me out...

274
00:20:21,440 --> 00:20:25,279
- Calm down, sit, and eat your mochi.
- Eating this isn't gonna calm me down!

275
00:20:25,280 --> 00:20:28,140
Why not? I bought that for you guys!

276
00:21:55,730 --> 00:21:59,150
It's already expired!

277
00:22:07,820 --> 00:22:10,360
Is your friend still at your place?

278
00:22:19,320 --> 00:22:20,520
Seriously...

279
00:22:21,250 --> 00:22:23,940
What am I even trying to do?

280
00:22:31,180 --> 00:22:34,390
(Kanda Satoshi: Can I count
on your help again this month?)

281
00:23:00,649 --> 00:23:02,364
(Kanda Eito: Is your
friend still at your place?)

282
00:23:02,408 --> 00:23:04,596
(Kanda Eito: I'm back from
my business trip to Sendai.)

283
00:23:24,320 --> 00:23:25,960
I need to find something to keep me busy.

284
00:23:28,840 --> 00:23:31,470
As long as I can live a
fulfilling life on my own,

285
00:23:32,460 --> 00:23:34,470
if I can just manage that,

286
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:41,040
there won't be any room for
feelings like love to sneak in.

287
00:23:44,880 --> 00:23:47,496
(Next Episode Preview) Someone
asked me to start a business with them.

288
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:49,820
Just seeing your face is
enough for me. I'm heading back.

289
00:23:50,400 --> 00:23:53,960
Truth is, someone I met
on a dating app came over.

290
00:23:54,620 --> 00:23:55,720
What is this feeling?

291
00:23:56,240 --> 00:23:59,310
I really just want Ueno
to spoil me right now.
